{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Hypothesis pass 2 + resolution (instrumentation path).\n\nSTRESS: 30 further iterations of the module under -n 4 --dist worksteal (210 fixture instantiations) on macOS/git 2.55 — all green. Combined with oropendola's ~29,400 executions, no organic reproduction exists.\n\nxdist worker-restart angle (evaluated, dead end): a crashed worker's basetemp rmtree could in principle race a sibling — but restarts require --max-worker-restart (not set; default = no restart), the failing run shows no worker crash, and each worker owns a disjoint popen-gwN basetemp. Also, the failing tmp dir (_0, first use) is created milliseconds before use with a unique name no other process learns, so cross-test targeted deletion is impossible; the deleter must be in-process, a git child, or ambient — all instrumentable.\n\nMECHANISM (proven by injection, deleter unidentified): unlinking the loose object between commit and merge reproduces the CI signature byte-for-byte (doubled 'invalid object' + 'fatal: git write-tree failed to write a tree', rc 128). Corrupt-but-present object => merge rc 0 (presence check is stat-only). hash-object confirms git add hashed correct bytes. So: ENOENT on a fresh loose object, cause unknown.\n\nLANDED (Gerrit change 1769): the ticket's instrumentation path. _GitFailed now carries an object-store forensics snapshot captured at failure time — git fsck --full, git count-objects -v, recursive .git/objects listing with sizes+mtimes, GIT_* environment — rendered in the exception, best-effort (capture failure never masks the original error), type stays CalledProcessError. Withheld-oracle TDD: regression test reproduces the proven mechanism (delete loose object -> merge) and went RED on each forensic section before the implementation; 4 manual mutants (no attach, no render, no fsck, no listing) all killed. make lint + make typecheck green. Next CI occurrence will name the missing objects, show what survived with mtimes, and rule env redirection in or out — pinning the deleter instead of restarting the hunt."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786691982106562001,"uuid":"35c6289a-d89f-4ffd-bc1a-a1606139d6f9"}